id: 11
hanzi: 猴子
pinyin: hóu zi
level: HSK 5
part_of_speech: Noun

meanings_summary:
  en: monkey; agile simian primate
  es: mono; simio ágil; primate de cola prensil o móvil

senses[1]{sense_number,part_of_speech,register,definition_en,definition_es,example_phrase}:
  1 | Noun | Standard | a small to medium-sized omnivorous primate with agile limbs and typically a long tail, known for its intelligence and dexterity | primate omnívoro de tamaño pequeño a mediano, extremidades ágiles y cola, conocido por su viveza e ingenio | 机灵的猴子 (clever monkey)

example_sentences[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 峨眉山林间的猴子非常调皮，不仅不怕游客，还经常成群结队地拦在路边索要各种坚果零食。 | Éméishān línjiān de hóuzi fēicháng tiáopí, bùjǐn bú pà yóukè, hái chángcháng chéngqún-jiéduì de lán zài lùbiān suǒyào gèzhǒng jiānguǒ língshí. | Monkeys in the forests of Mount Emei are mischievous; not fearing tourists, they often block paths in bands demanding nuts. | Los monos del bosque del monte Emei son traviesos; sin temer al caminante, interceptan la senda en tropel pidiendo frutos secos.
  #2 | 庄子寓言里的猴子因为主人朝四暮三的承诺而喜笑颜开，生动讽刺了世人被表象得失轻易愚弄的认知局限。 | Zhuāngzǐ yùyán lǐ de hóuzi yīnwèi zhǔrén zhāosì-mùsān de chéngnuò ér xǐxiào-yánkāi, shēngdòng fěngcì le shìrén bèi biǎoxiàng déshī qīngyì yúnòng de rènzhī júxiàn. | Monkeys in Zhuangzi's fable beamed joyously at the offer of four in morning and three at night, satirizing how easily humans are fooled by appearance. | Los monos de Zhuangzi sonrieron felices ante el reparto de cuatro bellotas al alba y tres al ocaso, satirizando la ingenuidad ante el espejismo de la ganancia.

collocations[6]{hanzi,en}:
  一只猴子 | a monkey (classifier: 只)
  猴子捞月 | monkeys fishing for the moon (futile pursuit)
  调皮的猴子 | mischievous, playful monkey
  猴子攀爬 | monkey climbing trees
  猴群领袖 | leader of the monkey troop
  金丝猴 | golden snub-nosed monkey (endangered species)

idioms[4]{hanzi,pinyin,meaning_en}:
  杀鸡儆猴 | shā jī jǐng hóu | kill the chicken to scare the monkey; punish one to warn hundreds
  尖嘴猴腮 | jiān zuǐ hóu sāi | sharp mouth and monkey cheeks; scrawny, treacherous look
  山中无老虎，猴子称大王 | shān zhōng wú lǎohǔ, hóuzi chēng dàiwáng | when tiger is away, monkey claims to be king
  沐猴而冠 | mù hóu ér guàn | a monkey wearing a hat; a scoundrel dressed in dignified robes

character_decomposition[2]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,meaning_es,radical,radical_meaning_en,meaning_component,sound_component,stroke_count,composition_type,etymology_and_mnemonic,visual_mnemonic_story_en,visual_mnemonic_story_es,tone_mnemonic_anchor,cangjie,traditional}:
  猴 | hóu | monkey; simian; clever child | mono; simio; niño travieso | 犭 | dog / wild beast | 犭 (wild animal / mammal) | 侯 (hóu, marquis / target / phonetic) | 12 | 左右结构 | Phono-semantic compound: animal radical 犭 paired with 侯 (marquis / nobleman), meaning the agile crowned marquis of primates. | A cunning wild beast (犭) crowned with the quick intelligence of an ancient marquis (侯) is an agile monkey (猴). | Una fiera ágil (犭) dotada de la presteza y noble ingenio de un marqués (侯) encarna al vivaz mono (猴). | 35 | KHNO | 
  子 | zi | child; son; noun suffix | hijo; niño; sufijo nominal | 子 | child / son | 子 (swaddled baby) | "" | 3 | 单一结构 | Universal nominalizing suffix in spoken Chinese used for animals, fruits, and everyday utensils. | An agile infant (子) waves small arms merrily, mimicking the lively leaps of a young primate. | Un infante travieso (子) agita las manos risueño imitando las cabriolas del monito. | 214 | ND | 

mnemonics_and_roots:
  composite_memory_hook_en: An agile wild beast (犭) with the cunning mind of a crowned marquis (侯) leaps through trees as a monkey (猴子).
  composite_memory_hook_es: Una criatura del bosque (犭) con el ingenio despierto de un marqués (侯) salta entre lianas como mono (猴子).
  cultural_and_cognitive_roots: In Chinese folklore (西游记), the monkey is immortalized by Sun Wukong (美猴王/齐天大圣), embodying rebellious wit, supernatural agility, and defiance of dogmatic authority. In classical Daoism, monkeys symbolize fickle perceptual desires easily appeased by superficial swaps.
  tone_sandhi_and_pitch_modulation: Rising 2nd tone followed by neutral tone: 'hóu zi' (35-neutral). Rise steadily on 'hóu' and pronounce 'zi' lightly without stress.

traps_and_cognates:
